WEBVTT

NOTE Automatically aligned; listening review pending.

line-1
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.400
I'm Bean, a little gray afternoon

line-2
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:08.820
I've got a blanket and a patch of room

line-3
00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:11.200
No great adventure on my mind

line-4
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:13.400
I've left that sort of thing behind

line-5
00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.740
You step toward me; I tiptoe away

line-6
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.720
Another cushion. Same lovely day

line-7
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.360
I've been awake for several minutes

line-8
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:25.720
You're still dreaming; I don't get it

line-9
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:27.800
I wait beside you, then I move

line-10
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.980
My little face right next to you

line-11
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.420
A purr, a meow, a second review

line-12
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.720
You chose a Bean. You knew what to do

line-13
00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.140
I'm not upset; I'm asking you

line-14
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:39.600
Did we forget that breakfast was due?

line-15
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.320
You stir; I follow down the hall

line-16
00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:43.840
That little silver lid says it all

line-17
00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.660
One soft click, and I know it's true

line-18
00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:47.680
My favorite kind of love comes through

line-19
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:49.940
Breakfast was due

line-20
00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.340
And the morning came through

line-21
00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:56.720
Warm in my corner, with nothing to prove

line-22
00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.380
A bowl of something lovely

line-23
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:01.440
A blanket made for two

line-24
00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.180
A little space, a little grace

line-25
00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:05.900
And love that lets me choose

line-26
00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:07.260
Breakfast was due

line-27
00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:10.460
Salmon, tuna, chicken too

line-28
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.820
I hear that can and fall for you

line-29
00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:15.080
Your boys leave kibble; I believe

line-30
00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.180
Good food was never meant to grieve

line-31
00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.380
They call me Foopa Master; fair

line-32
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.420
I wear them round and doing fine

line-34
00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.840
The soft life suits this shape of mine

line-35
00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.660
My brothers bring their big ideas

line-36
00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:28.960
I hiss; they don't appear to hear

line-37
00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.260
I lose, then find another seat

line-39
00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:33.540
My afternoon was going well

line-40
00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.880
I've nothing more to prove or tell

line-41
00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.260
I may step back when you come near

line-42
00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.520
It doesn't mean I want you gone

line-43
00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:42.860
At night I climb the blanket here

line-44
00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:45.120
And press my little paws along

line-45
00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.440
I know it's you beneath the fold

line-46
00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.720
I like the quiet that we share

line-47
00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:52.360
I needn't ask for you to hold me

line-48
00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:54.400
I like knowing you are there

line-49
00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:56.580
Was that the kitchen?

line-50
00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:57.740
Breakfast was due

line-51
00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.240
And the morning came through

line-52
00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.780
Warm in my corner, with nothing to prove

line-53
00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:06.340
My bowl is empty now

line-54
00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.240
My brothers found something to do

line-55
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:10.520
A little space, a little grace

line-56
00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.280
And love that lets me choose

line-57
00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:13.920
I'm your Foopa Master

line-58
00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.260
With a blanket and a view

line-59
00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:17.620
Breakfast was due

line-60
00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.260
I curl up, then I tiptoe free

line-61
00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:22.540
You lift me: I'm the Dancing Queen

line-62
00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:24.280
I had intended just to sit

line-63
00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.340
I suppose I'll live with it

line-64
00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:27.460
...Clarence Thomas.
